From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 08:59:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 142/185] Clear the drive-state mask per round, and what round
 1 says

The patience change landed. Round 1 with DRV_INIT on came back "bad 4
0302" -- stage 3, where the last two hardware runs gave stage 2 at
state 8. Stage 3 is past brd_wait_init, and that gate only opens on
drive state 1, 2 or 4. So DRV_INIT does revive this drive; it needed
twenty seconds and was being given three and a third.

What still fails is the read after it: ROMREADN announces no sector
inside its own fresh 200 frames, with the drive sitting at state 2 the
whole time.

Meanwhile cdd_statemask cannot answer the one question left, because
it accumulates over the session: the 0, 6 and 7 the boot probe
collected are still in it an hour later, so no later round can ever
show a clean sheet no matter what the drive is doing. Clear it in
segacd_cd_revive(), which already means "this round starts fresh".
cdd_first stays session-wide -- the first state EmuTOS ever heard is a
fact about the handover, not about a round.
---
 bios/scdapi.h |  4 ++--
 bios/segacd.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/scdapi.h b/bios/scdapi.h
index 1abab03..174683a 100644
--- a/bios/scdapi.h
+++ b/bios/scdapi.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 #define SCDAPI_H
 
 #define SCD_COOKIE   0x53674344L        /* 'SgCD' */
-#define SCD_VERSION  10
+#define SCD_VERSION  11
 
 /* Everything the disc diagnostic prints, in one go. Taken in a single
  * call rather than twenty accessors so that the numbers in one report
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@ struct scd_snap {
 #define SCD_BIOS_READTEST 5             /* -> 0 if the firmware read a sector */
 #define SCD_BIOS_NEARREAD 6             /* -> ...one it read at boot */
 #define SCD_BIOS_SWAPS    7             /* -> how many exchanges have run */
-#define SCD_REVIVE        8             /* the drive gets another chance */
+#define SCD_REVIVE        8             /* another chance, and a clean mask */
 
 struct scd_api {
     unsigned short size;                /* sizeof(struct scd_api) */
diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 527f502..8990254 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -3071,6 +3071,18 @@ void segacd_cd_revive(void)
 {
     cd_deadrun = 0;
     cd_dead = 0;
+
+    /* And forget which drive states have been seen.
+     *
+     * cdd_statemask accumulates over the whole session, so the 0, 6 and
+     * 7 the boot probe collected are still in it an hour later and no
+     * later round can ever report a clean sheet. That made the mask
+     * useless for the question it was added to answer -- whether our
+     * own CDD conversation can see a live drive once something else has
+     * woken it. Per round, it can. cdd_first is deliberately left
+     * alone: "the first state EmuTOS ever heard" is a fact about the
+     * handover and belongs to the session. */
+    cdd_statemask = 0;
 }
 
 /* deskmain() has been entered: the boot's short leash is over.
